      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_5fe234b4c780152a65a77b273f97f2920c33da6357c469280f864d974212bcb2",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Curvature does not directly cancel the exponential sum here. It makes the derivative monotone and controls how long the phase can remain near an integer resonance. The proof therefore decomposes the obstruction into a small number of narrow bad regions and complementary regions where first-derivative separation is effective.",
